        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63251,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fallopian tube</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63252,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tubo-ovarian abscess classically presents as an adnexal mass (often bilateral), with fever, lower abdominal or pelvic pain, vaginal discharge, and leukocytosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63253,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tubo-ovarian abscesses occur in women of reproductive age after upper genital tract infection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63254,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tubo-ovarian abscess is a late complication of pelvic inflammatory disease. It is often polymicrobial, typically containing anaerobic bacteria; <em>Actinomyces</em> and mycobacteria can be causative. There is an association with instrumentation and diabetes {28290977; 26607184; 12459228; 27178227}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63255,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tubo-ovarian abscess may be associated with endometriosis and rarely with an intrauterine device.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63256,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is marked distortion of tubal and ovarian anatomy.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63257,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is destructive acute and chronic inflammation, necrosis, abscess formation, and fibrosis involving the fallopian tube and the ovary. Coexistent endometriosis may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63258,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63259,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63260,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> inflammation involving tube and ovary.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:35:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
